From: HakiOS
Subject: [PATCH 0166] sweet: AMP scheduling (A76 = P, A55 = E) and no timer coalescing


Profiles of 0172p/0172m: neither CoreAnimation's render thread (32 % running), SpringBoard's
main thread (16 %) nor the GPU (40-60 % busy) is saturated, yet frames are 36 ms apart:
latency, not throughput. The kernel scheduled all eight cores as one SMP cluster, so UI
threads ran on Cortex-A55s as often as on the A76s.

- SWEET.h __ARM_AMP__ 1, board_config MAX_CPU_CLUSTERS 2: sched_amp with an E pset (cpu0-5)
  and a P pset (cpu6-7). The ADT must carry the cluster types (tools/mkadt.py --amp,
  SWEET_AMP=1 in tools/sweet-gpu-image.sh); this kernel is not meant for the SMP ADT.
- sched_amp spill/idle-steal/spill-steal thresholds -32 on SWEET (Apple's 3/1/1 kept UI bursts
  queued on the two A76s: DC28088/ios-sweet 0248 and its NOTES 2026-11-11, ~30 -> ~45 fps
  with -32 on this SoC). kern.sched_amp_* sysctls still change them.
- Timer coalescing off at boot (mach_timer_coalescing_enabled); boot-arg sweet_coal=1
  restores Apple's default.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/kern/sched_amp_common.c b/osfmk/kern/sched_amp_common.c
index 3c0974a..a7f59fe 100644
--- a/osfmk/kern/sched_amp_common.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/sched_amp_common.c
@@ -65,9 +65,20 @@ sched_amp_init(void)
 }
 
 /* Spill threshold load average is ncpus in pset + (sched_amp_spill_count/(1 << PSET_LOAD_FRACTIONAL_SHIFT) */
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+/*
+ * 0166: two P cores only. With Apple's 3/1/1 the lagging P load average kept UI bursts queued on
+ * the two A76s while A55s idled (DC28088 2482: more missed frames); -32 makes the gate the run
+ * queue alone (their 2482 + live -32: ~30 -> ~45 frames a second). Still kern.sched_amp_* sysctls.
+ */
+int sched_amp_spill_count = -32;
+int sched_amp_idle_steal = -32;
+int sched_amp_spill_steal = -32;
+#else
 int sched_amp_spill_count = 3;
 int sched_amp_idle_steal = 1;
 int sched_amp_spill_steal = 1;
+#endif
 
 /*
  * We see performance gains from doing immediate IPIs to P-cores to run
diff --git a/osfmk/kern/timer_call.c b/osfmk/kern/timer_call.c
index f8c8180..31da18c 100644
--- a/osfmk/kern/timer_call.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/timer_call.c
@@ -265,6 +265,18 @@ timer_call_init(void)
 {
 	timer_longterm_init();
 	timer_call_init_abstime();
+#if defined(ARM64_BOARD_CONFIG_SWEET)
+	/*
+	 * 0166: no timer coalescing (DC28088 measured 1 ms sleeps waking ~19 ms late with it on this
+	 * SoC). Boot-arg sweet_coal=1 restores Apple's default; kern.timer_coalescing_enabled too.
+	 */
+	{
+		uint32_t coal = 0;
+
+		(void)PE_parse_boot_argn("sweet_coal", &coal, sizeof(coal));
+		mach_timer_coalescing_enabled = coal != 0;
+	}
+#endif
 }
 
 
diff --git a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/SWEET.h b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/SWEET.h
index b99c2f4..8c35b68 100644
--- a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/SWEET.h
+++ b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/SWEET.h
@@ -25,6 +25,14 @@
  */
 #define SWEET_SMP_MAX_CPUS         8
 
+/*
+ * 0166: AMP (after DC28088/ios-sweet 0248). With MAX_CPU_CLUSTERS 2 and the ADT's cluster
+ * types, ml_parse_cpu_topology makes an E pset (cpu0-5) and a P pset (cpu6-7) and sched_amp
+ * puts user threads above utility QoS on the A76s, spilling to the A55s (spill thresholds:
+ * sched_amp_common.c, 0166).
+ */
+#define __ARM_AMP__               1
+
 #define ARM_ARCH_TIMER
 #define __ARM_ARCH__              8
 #define __ARM_VMSA__              8
diff --git a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/board_config.h b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/board_config.h
index 88e524a..d55c930 100644
--- a/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/board_config.h
+++ b/pexpert/pexpert/arm64/board_config.h
@@ -102,7 +102,9 @@
 
 #define MAX_L2_CLINE                   6
 #define MAX_CPUS                       8
-#define MAX_CPU_CLUSTERS               1
+/* 0166: two clusters (six Cortex-A55 = E, two Cortex-A76 = P) for XNU's sched_amp; the ADT must
+ * say so (tools/mkadt.py --amp): cpu0-5 cluster-type 'E', cpu6-7 'P' */
+#define MAX_CPU_CLUSTERS               2
 
 #define CORE_NCTRS                     8 /* Placeholder; KPC is not enabled for this target */
 
